c GPT solve time: 142.55 seconds

STEP-BY-STEP DPLL-STYLE OUTLINE:

1) PARSE AND INITIALIZE
   • Read all clauses (already in CNF).  
   • No unit clauses initially, so no immediate forced assignments.  
   • Keep an empty partial assignment; set “branches” and “conflicts” counters to zero.

2) CHOOSE A LITERAL AND BRANCH
   Example of a common branching order (though many heuristics are possible): pick the lowest-index variable not yet assigned.  
   a) Assign x₁ = True (branches = 1).  
   b) Perform unit propagation (i.e., check if this forces other variables). If a conflict arises, backtrack, increment “conflicts,” and flip x₁ to False. If still conflicting, backtrack further.  
   c) Otherwise, pick the next unassigned variable (say x₂), set x₂ = False (branches++), propagate, handle conflicts similarly.  
   d) Continue in this manner until all variables are assigned or until all branches are exhausted.

3) UNIT PROPAGATION AND CONFLICTS
   • Whenever a literal in a clause becomes True by the partial assignment, that clause is automatically satisfied.  
   • If, for a given clause, all but one literal become False, the remaining literal must be True to satisfy that clause (this is the usual “unit clause” propagation).  
   • If ever a clause has all its literals assigned False, that is a conflict: increment “conflicts,” backtrack to the last branching point, flip that choice, and propagate again.

4) TERMINATION
   • If all clauses can be satisfied under some complete assignment, the formula is SATISFIABLE.  
   • If every branch leads to a conflict, the formula is UNSATISFIABLE.

